# EditVault GitHub account (3rd account)

This project may use a **separate GitHub account** labeled **editvault**. The user has **other git accounts** (Gitea + another GitHub) — **never modify their SSH config, remotes, or credentials**.

## Before any GitHub action

**Always ask the user first** before:
- `git push`, `git pull`, `git fetch`, or changing `origin`
- `gh auth login`, `gh repo create`, `gh pr create`, or any `gh` command targeting GitHub
- Editing `~/.ssh/config` entries other than `github-editvault`
- Switching git user.name / user.email for commits

## When approved, use only the editvault identity

- SSH remote: `git@github-editvault:USERNAME/REPO.git` (Host alias `github-editvault`)
- Key file: `~/.ssh/id_ed25519_editvault` — do not reuse default `id_ed25519`
- Push frequency: occasional only — do not push unless the user asks

## Do not touch

- Other SSH hosts in `~/.ssh/config` (plesk, ubuntu, Ginx, Benny, etc.)
- Other GitHub/Gitea remotes or credentials on this machine
